  "hostNotes": "Jokes are fine to accept as long as they are something you could plausibly find in, on, or shortly after a servo pie: regret, lava, a horse and a Band-Aid all score like any other answer, and the gross ones are deliberately tiered rare/deep so a lone joker gets rewarded. Bare 'sauce' means tomato sauce (on top) and still counts; 'salt and pepper' said together scores as Salt; 'dead horse' is sauce, not horse; 'pepper steak' is Steak. Known near-synonyms are pre-merged (gristle absorbs cartilage/sinew/tendon, potato absorbs mash, steak absorbs chunky/pepper steak, preservatives absorbs chemicals/numbers/additives, molten centre absorbs both the lava jokes and the frozen-middle complaints); Meat, Beef and Mince are kept separate because the room will say all three, so only collapse them if the table agrees two players meant the same thing."
}
